Touchscreen driver for the Google Pixel 7

The driver 'ft3658_touch' is a port of the vendor's Linux driver for the
FocalTech FT3658U touchscreen, attached via the vendor's SPI controller
driver. It provides the touches as an Event session. It needs the ports
'pixel_linux', 'google_soc_gs', 'google_touch', and 'google_display'.

The scenario 'run/ft3658_touch_pixel' logs the touches via 'event_dump':

! make run/ft3658_touch_pixel KERNEL=hw BOARD=google_pixel7
